635
01:13:16,226 --> 01:13:22,574
''Hanuman was an eternal
devotee of Lord Rama''

636
01:13:22,666 --> 01:13:29,060
He approaches Rama to quench
his life long thirst

637
01:13:29,306 --> 01:13:34,903
''O'' Rama. . Lord Rama''

638
01:13:38,826 --> 01:13:42,023
''Taking Rama and Laxman
on his shoulders. . ''

639
01:13:42,106 --> 01:13:45,018
Hanuman lands on a mountain

640
01:13:45,186 --> 01:13:51,659
''He introduces them to Sugriv
who was fed up with Vali''

641
01:13:55,026 --> 01:14:01,261
''Because of Hanuman,
Sugriv gained''

642
01:14:07,746 --> 01:14:11,022
''When the trees were felled
with one single arrow. . ''

643
01:14:11,106 --> 01:14:17,022
. .Vali was killed. .
Vali was killed

644
01:14:17,106 --> 01:14:20,178
Long live Lord Rama

645
01:14:20,266 --> 01:14:26,501
''They all thought and realised
the greatness of Lord Rama''

646
